  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Group's Caderneta",
    "overview": "A calm, familiar team app on a flat near-black green ground, where the players are cromos: white-framed 3:4 stickers with a photo or initials on green and the name in condensed caps. The chrome stays quiet and conventional (cards, a bottom bar, two answer buttons) so that the one invented object, the cromo, carries the identity. Opening a group shows when the next game is, whose cromo is already stuck in, and which slots still say \"Falta\".\n\nDensity is phone-first and compact: 15px base text, 16px gaps between sections, a 5-column cromo grid. Colour is spent by meaning, not decoration: grass answers, lime points at the user, gold rewards. The system refuses the \"AI sports app\" default of radial glows, glowing gradient buttons, pitch-stripe heroes and tracked uppercase labels.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Flat dark-green ground with bordered cards; no ambient glows.",
      "The cromo (3:4, white frame, condensed name) is the signature object.",
      "Barlow for interface text, Barlow Condensed 800 for numbers, dates and cromo names.",
      "Each accent has one job; rarity keeps lime and gold legible.",
      "One authored motion: the cromo \"sticks\" onto the page."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Job Rule",
        "body": "Lime means \"you need to act\", gold means \"earned\". Neither is used as decoration or as a generic highlight.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Grass Answers Rule",
        "body": "The single filled green button on a screen is the user's answer. Everything else is ghost, link or tinted.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence-Case Label Rule",
        "body": "Section labels are 13px semibold dim text in sentence case. Uppercase belongs only to condensed numerals, dates, opponents and cromo names.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Condensed Is For Facts Rule",
        "body": "Barlow Condensed sets numbers, dates and names, never running copy or buttons.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
